<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Colline Gate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">82 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sullas-civil-war">Sulla's civil war</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Colline Gate was fought on 1 November 82 BCE outside the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>'s army defeated a force of Samnites and Lucanians led by Pontius Telesinus, fighting with Roman opponents of Sulla, in a hard battle that lasted into the night, after which Sulla had thousands of prisoners killed. The victory ended the civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and made Sulla dictator.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-colline-gate.jpg" alt="Battle of the Colline Gate" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The British Library · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_British_Library_-_Rome_-_Porta_Collina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
